The attached image, Figure 5, illustrates that Nano-11 significantly enhances the uptake of adsorbed antigens by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs). Panel (A) displays flow cytometry dot plots, showing minimal soluble ovalbumin (OVA) uptake by BMDCs, but a substantial increase in OVA uptake when combined with Nano-11, with both colocalizing within cells. Panel (B), a histogram for FITC-OVA, quantitatively confirms this, with a pronounced shift to higher fluorescence for Nano-11+OVA compared to OVA alone. This enhanced antigen delivery to DCs is a crucial mechanism by which Nano-11 functions as an effective vaccine adjuvant.